<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally lower on moderate demand and moderate to heavy offerings. Select and Choice rib, round and loin cuts mostly weak, while chuck cuts lower. Beef trimmings lower on moderate demand and fairly heavy offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>-----</p>
<p>323 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 88 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>22 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     106.41	105.85	101.21	100.68</p>
<p>Changes	  -1.07	 -0.83	 -0.98	 -0.86</p>
<p>Rib	  160.39	159.06	149.14	148.07</p>
<p>Chuck	 74.09	 71.44	 73.98	 71.74</p>
<p>Round	 92.27	 92.27	 89.51	 89.51</p>
<p>Loin	 168.64	170.43	152.99	154.22</p>
<p>Brisket     61.26	 61.26	 60.61	 60.61</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  72.17	 72.07	 72.46	 72.25</p>
<p>Flank	 60.57	 60.57	 61.21	 61.21</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
